R"VG(
# manual.vg (H-04, the second pass): the manual: the people's own machines (their stoves burn their fuel, their mills grind their crop,
# their machines do their crafts), step by step, and the warnings. A step is built from parts (the action, the part, the manner), each
# people's makers with their own few ways of saying each, so two peoples' manuals for one stove read apart.

genre.manual (words=29..85)
  {man.head}\n{man.step}\n{man.step}\n{man.step}\n{man.step}\n{man.warn}
  {man.head}\n{man.intro}\n{man.step}\n{man.step}\n{man.step}\n{man.warn}
  {man.head}\n{man.step}\n{man.step}\n{man.step}\n{man.fault}\n{man.warn}

man.head (formula people=3)
  Instructions for the use of the {man.thing}. Read before use.
  The {man.thing}: operating instructions.
  How to use your {man.thing}.
  The {man.thing}. Keep these instructions with the unit.
  Your new {man.thing}, and how to look after it.

man.thing (keep people=4)
  water purifier{=.mt:water}
  generator{=.mt:fuel}
  stove{=.mt:fuel}
  pump{=.mt:water}
  heater{=.mt:fuel}
  sewing machine{=.mt:none}
  bicycle{=.mt:none}
  washing machine{=.mt:water}
  cold box{=.mt:none}
  water heater{=.mt:water}
  {fuel} heater{=.mt:fuel}
  {craft} machine{=.mt:none}
  {crop} mill{=.mt:grain}
  (inv.radio=1) radio receiver{=.mt:none}
  (inv.computer=1) terminal{=.mt:none}
  (inv.telephone=1) telephone{=.mt:none}

man.intro (share=0.8)
  Thank you for choosing this {man.thing}, made in {$home}.
  This {man.thing} was made at the {craft} works in {$home} and should last a lifetime.
  Please read all of this before you begin, {man.intro2}.
  Your {man.thing} has been tested at the works {man.intro3}.
man.intro2 (people=3)
  including the warnings
  even if you have used one before
  slowly
  and keep it somewhere dry
  with someone who has used one
  and keep it for the next owner
man.intro3 (people=2)
  and passed
  by hand
  three times
  and found sound

man.step
  (once) {man.v.check} the {man.part} {man.when}.
  (once) Turn the {man.knob} {man.dir} until {man.until}.
  (once .mt=water|.mt=fuel|.mt=grain) Fill the {man.tank} with {man.fill} {man.fillto}.
  (once) Clean the {man.filter} {man.with} once a {man.period}{man.more}.
  (once) If the unit {man.noise}, {man.react}.
  (once) Keep the unit {man.keep}{man.keep2}.
  (once .mt!=none) Never put {man.never} in the {man.part2}.
  (once) Wait {#n|minute} before you {man.next}.
  (once) Oil the {man.part} with {man.oil} every {man.period}.
  (once) Stand the unit on {man.surface}, away from {man.away}.
  (once) The {man.part} must face {man.face}.
  (once) Do not leave the {man.thing} {man.leave}.
  (once) {man.firstw}, make sure the unit is {man.first}.

man.v.check (people=3)
  Check
  Inspect
  Look at
  Feel
  Test
  Tighten
  Wipe
man.when (people=3)
  before each use
  every {man.period}
  when the unit is cold
  after {season.now}
  once the light is out
  when you first unpack it
man.knob (people=3)
  dial
  handle
  lever
  wheel
  red knob
  brass key
man.dir (people=2)
  to the right
  to the left
  a quarter turn
  slowly, one notch at a time
man.until (people=3)
  the light comes on
  it clicks
  the needle reaches the mark
  the hum stops
  you feel it catch
man.tank (people=2)
  tank
  reservoir
  drum
  bowl
  hopper
man.fill
  (.mt=water) clean water
  (.mt=water) water from the {watersrc.n}
  (.mt=fuel) {fuel}
  (.mt=grain) {crop}
man.fillto (people=2)
  to the line, and no further
  until it is half full
  a little at a time
  through the funnel provided
man.filter (people=2)
  filter
  grate
  screen
  outlet
  sieve
man.with (people=2)
  with a dry cloth
  with warm water
  with a soft brush
  with {drink}, if nothing else is to hand
man.more (people=3)
  (2)
  , or more often in {season.now}
  , or when it smells
  , whether it needs it or not
man.period
  month
  week
  season
  year
man.noise (people=3)
  makes a noise
  smells of burning
  shakes
  stops for no reason
  runs hot
  sings
man.react (people=3)
  switch it off and {man.call}
  stand back and wait
  do not hit it
  open the window
  {man.call}
man.call (people=2)
  call the service number
  ask at the works
  call a qualified engineer
  send for the makers
  wait for it to cool before you touch anything
man.keep (people=3)
  dry
  clean
  away from children
  out of the sun
  away from {herd}
man.keep2 (people=2)
  (2)
  , and the cover on
  , and the door shut
  , and its instructions with it
man.part (people=4)
  belt
  hose
  seal
  plug
  chain
  valve
  lid
  spring
  gasket
  drive wheel
man.part2 (people=2)
  tank
  filter
  outlet
  drum
man.never
  (.mt!=fuel) {fuel}
  (.mt!=water) water from the {watersrc.n}
  anything sharp
  {drink}
  {food}
  your fingers
man.next (people=4)
  open the cover
  touch the {man.part}
  switch it on again
  (.mt=fuel) add more {fuel}
  call the works
  move it
  empty the {man.tank}
man.oil (people=2)
  a little grease
  lamp oil
  a drop of fat
  the oil supplied
  a feather dipped in oil
man.surface (people=2)
  a flat floor
  a stone slab
  a level table
  the stand provided
man.away (people=3)
  the curtains
  the {herd}
  the stove
  children
  the bed
  anything made of {material}
man.face (people=2)
  the wall
  the window
  the north
  the door
man.leave (people=3)
  running overnight
  in the rain
  where children can reach it
  full
  with the cover off
man.firstw (people=2)
  First
  Before anything else
  To begin
  Always
  Each time
man.first (people=3)
  switched off
  cold
  standing level
  empty
  unplugged
  out of the sun

man.fault (share=0.7)
  If it will not start, check the {man.part} first; it is nearly always the {man.part}.
  If the light flashes, the {man.tank} is empty, or the {man.part} is loose.
  If it hums but nothing happens, wait, then try again, then call the works.
  If it {man.noise}, the {man.part} has worn; a new one costs {#n} {coin} at the works.

man.warn
  Warning: {man.danger}.
  Keep these instructions. {man.warn2}
  The makers accept no responsibility for {man.misuse}.
  Spare parts from {man.spare} only{man.spare2}.
  The guarantee does not cover {weather}, or {man.misuse}.
man.spare2
  (2)
  , and only with the receipt
  , whatever the market says
  , or the guarantee is void
man.spare (people=2)
  the works at {$home}
  the {craft} guild's shops
  an approved dealer
  the makers
man.danger (people=4)
  do not use near water
  hot surfaces
  do not run it indoors
  this is not a toy
  keep it away from {fuel}
  do not open the cover while it runs
  dangerous to {herd}
  do not use it in {weather.now}
man.warn2 (people=2)
  Nobody does, but keep them.
  You will want them in {season.next}.
  They are the only copy the works will send.
man.misuse (people=3)
  misuse
  use by children
  use with {fuel}
  damage by {herd}
  a hammer
)VG"
